# Page Naming Convention

Page and step component naming conventions for `src/pages/`.

## Page Components

- **All page components must use `Page` suffix** - `DashboardPage`, `PayrollOnboardingPage`, `SettingsPage`
- Component files use PascalCase - `DashboardPage.tsx`, `PayrollOnboardingPage.tsx`

## Step Components

- **All step components must use `Step` suffix** - `WelcomeStep`, `CompanyInfoStep`, `TaxSetupStep`
- Component files use PascalCase - `WelcomeStep.tsx`, `CompanyInfoStep.tsx`

## Directory Names

- **Page directories use lowercase or kebab-case** - `payroll/`, `payroll/onboarding/`, `payroll/employees/`
- Do not use PascalCase for directories - not `PayrollOnboarding/` or `CustomerWizard/`
- Related features can nest under a parent directory - `payroll/employees/`, `payroll/timesheets/`

## Main Entry File Naming

- The main entry file in a folder-based page uses a descriptive PascalCase name with `Page` suffix
- Folder `payroll/onboarding/` -> `PayrollOnboardingPage.tsx`
- Folder `payroll/employees/` -> `PayrollEmployeesPage.tsx`

## Prohibited Names

- **No generic names** - Do not use `Page.tsx`, `Index.tsx`, `Main.tsx`, or `Step.tsx` as primary identifiers
- Do not use page or step components without the required suffix

## Summary

| Type        | Naming Rule    | Example                    |
|-------------|----------------|----------------------------|
| Page file   | PascalCase + Page | `DashboardPage.tsx`     |
| Step file   | PascalCase + Step | `WelcomeStep.tsx`      |
| Page folder | lowercase / kebab-case | `payroll/onboarding/`  |
| Entry file  | PascalCase + Page | `PayrollOnboardingPage.tsx` |
